@startuml Browser Operational Lifecycle and Revocation
autonumber
skinparam actorStyle AWESOME

skinparam BoxPadding 10

actor "Practitioner" as User
participant "Angular Application" as UI
participant "Nginx Gateway" as Nginx
participant "oauth2-proxy" as Proxy
participant "Node.js BFF" as BFF
participant "Redis Cache" as Redis
participant "Keycloak IdP" as KC
participant "HAPI FHIR Server" as FHIR

== 1. API Scoped Request & Silent Token Refresh ==
User -> UI : Initiate Clinical Resource Access Request
UI -> Nginx : GET the needed api endpoint
Nginx -> Proxy : Evaluate Cookie Expiration

alt Access Token Nearing Expiry Window
    Proxy -> KC : POST /token (Execute Refresh via Refresh Token)
    KC --> Proxy : Return Refreshed Token Cluster
    Proxy -> Proxy : Re-encrypt Storage Context into Updated Cookie
end

Proxy -> Nginx : Inject Bearer Access Token Header
Nginx -> BFF : Proxied Request + Bearer Token Context
BFF -> BFF : Perform Consent & Scope Checks

alt Capability Present in Memory Cache
    BFF -> Redis : Query Patient Data Cache
    Redis --> BFF : Return Valid Authorization Capability
else Cache Miss / Direct Query Required
    BFF -> FHIR : Forward Authorized Request
    activate FHIR
    FHIR --> BFF : Return Medical Record JSON
    deactivate FHIR
    BFF -> Redis : Persist Record inside Cache
end

BFF --> Nginx : Return Response Data
Nginx --> UI : Forward Response
UI -> User : Render Medical Data Interface View

== 2. Multi-Tiered Synchronized Global Logout ==
User -> UI : Trigger "Logout of All Devices"
UI -> Nginx : POST /auth/logout-global
Nginx -> Proxy : Clear Gateway Session Cookie
Proxy -> Nginx : Clear-Cookie Instruction Headers
Nginx -> BFF : Route Invalidation Hook Context
BFF -> KC : POST /admin/realms/{realm}/users/{id}/logout
KC --> BFF : User Sessions Invalidated
BFF -> Redis : Flush Active Sessions ma User IDtching User ID
BFF --> Nginx : Global Logout Resolved (200 OK)
Nginx --> UI : Forward Acknowledgement
' UI -> UI : Purge Client Cryptographic Buffers
UI -> User : Redirect to authentication page
@enduml